      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think adding the try-catch is the right direction. However, even if the HID connection fails, I think we should print the error log and keep the session valid with the video connection at least.\n\nIf the video connection fails, RFB_CLIENT_REFUSE makes sense. But if the HID connection fails, I think it would be better to print the error log and continue with RFB_CLIENT_ACCEPT. Our code already supports running with the HID fd set to -1.",
      "revId": "bfc388ff71a1f8fa89f1dc3d552b02cb19499550",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
